# Complete Code

```python
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression


# =========================================================
# PART 1: LOAD DATASET
# =========================================================

# CSV file ko read karke DataFrame mein store kar rahe hain
df = pd.read_csv('/content/california_housing_train.csv')


# =========================================================
# PART 2: FEATURE AND TARGET
# =========================================================

# X = Feature/Input
# Longitude ko input feature bana rahe hain
X = df[['longitude']]

# y = Target/Output
# Latitude ko target bana rahe hain
y = df['latitude']


# =========================================================
# PART 3: LINEAR REGRESSION MODEL
# =========================================================

# Linear Regression model create karna
model = LinearRegression()

# Model ko Longitude aur Latitude ka relationship sikhana
model.fit(X, y)


# =========================================================
# PART 4: PREDICTION
# =========================================================

# Trained model se Latitude ki predicted values nikalna
prediction = model.predict(X)


# =========================================================
# PART 5: 99th PERCENTILE / OUTLIERS
# =========================================================

# Longitude ki 99th percentile limit
x_limit = df['longitude'].quantile(0.99)

# Latitude ki 99th percentile limit
y_limit = df['latitude'].quantile(0.99)


# =========================================================
# PART 6: FILTER OUTLIERS
# =========================================================

# Sirf woh rows rakhenge jahan:
# Longitude x_limit se kam ho
# AND
# Latitude y_limit se kam ho

df_clean = df[
    (df['longitude'] < x_limit) &
    (df['latitude'] < y_limit)
]


# =========================================================
# PART 7: CLEAN DATA
# =========================================================

# Clean data ka Feature
x_clean = df_clean[['longitude']]

# Clean data ka Target
y_clean = df_clean['latitude']


# =========================================================
# PART 8: NEW MODEL ON CLEAN DATA
# =========================================================

# Clean data ke liye naya Linear Regression model
model_clean = LinearRegression()

# Clean data par model train karna
model_clean.fit(x_clean, y_clean)

# Clean data ki prediction
prediction_clean = model_clean.predict(x_clean)


# =========================================================
# PART 9: SUBPLOT
# =========================================================

# Figure ka size set karna
plt.figure(figsize=(12, 5))


# ---------------- ORIGINAL DATA ----------------

# First subplot
plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)

# Original actual data
plt.scatter(X, y, color='blue', alpha=0.3)

# Original regression line
plt.plot(X, prediction, color='red')

plt.xlabel('Longitude')
plt.ylabel('Latitude')
plt.title('Original Data')


# ---------------- CLEAN DATA ----------------

# Second subplot
plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)

# Outliers filter karne ke baad actual data
plt.scatter(x_clean, y_clean, color='blue', alpha=0.3)

# Clean data ki regression line
plt.plot(x_clean, prediction_clean, color='red')

plt.xlabel('Longitude')
plt.ylabel('Latitude')
plt.title('After Removing Outliers')


# Graphs ki spacing adjust karna
plt.tight_layout()

# Graph show karna
plt.show()
```

## One-Line Revision 🧠

```text
Dataset → X/y select → Model create → fit() → predict()
        → 99% limit → Outliers filter → New model
        → Original vs Clean Data subplot
```

**Important:** `df_clean` banana **data filtering** hai, jabki `plt.xlim()` / `plt.ylim()` sirf **graph ki visible range** change karte hain.
